Here is my expert advice:

Bless that magic lamp and wish for an uncursed magic marker. Assuming
you have maxxed your luck, you can write any scroll or spellbook with
extremely low chance of failure.  If you have done anything that might
hurt your luck (i.e. killing a lot of guards), fix it before you try
to wish or write unknown scrolls/spellbooks.

Here is what you will write, if possible:

1) blessed ?of charging
2) blessed +of charm monster
3) cursed ?SoGeno

other optional things to write include:
4) +of identify
5) +of haste self (better than speed boots for a wiz, IMHO)
6) +of jumping ( for quick getaways )

and of course

7) b?of enchant armor

You are going to reverse genocide silver dragons.  Since this is
dangerous, you will do this in a small room (at least 3x3) with the
door blocked by a boulder.  Before reading the scroll, use Magicbane
to engrave ElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElbereth on every
square in the room.  Use caution in melee, check the engraving every
few hits, and add an extra Elbereth whenever one gets messed up.
Once you have the silver scales, you should charm the other dragons. 
Then you should eat one of the dragon corpses for cold resistance if
you don't have that yet ( get un-satiated before fighting those
dragons ).  Enchant those scales and ditch the mithril.

Get a stack of 8-12 daggers.  You are expert in dagger, and you need a
ranged attack that doesn't require magic.  12 daggers might be enough
for a guard captain.  If not, bounce a magic missile as well.  Don't
engage in melee combat with tough monsters if you can avoid it.

Killing the guards will hurt your luck and alignment.  Be sure you can
fix it soon afterwards.

If you find a magic marker before you bless the lamp, you might wish
for the Master Key of Thievery.  It gives you teleport control and
half phys-damage.

